course: dictionary
lesson: 16171
title: Wrongful and the law
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words are built from a shorter word you already know. Wrongful comes from wrong, and it means unfair, unjust or against the law. «The judge said the arrest was wrongful, because the police had no proof.» The word wrong is a clue, and the sentence tells you the arrest was unfair.
explain: Look at the words around it too. «Ava had been at school all day, so the accusation that she broke the window was wrongful.» Ava was at school, so she could not have done it. That means blaming her was unfair. Try your meaning in the sentence: «the accusation was unfair» still makes sense, so you have it right.
explain: Wrongful is a formal word, so you will mostly meet it in law and news. You may hear wrongful arrest, when someone is arrested unfairly, or wrongful dismissal, when someone is sacked unfairly. A wrongful act is not just a bad act. It is one that breaks the rules of fairness or the law.
fact: Wrongful means unfair, unjust or against the law.
fact: Wrongful comes from wrong, and the ending -ful means full of.
fact: «Wrongful arrest» means being arrested unfairly or against the law.
fact: «Wrongful dismissal» means being sacked from a job unfairly or against the law.
fact: Wrongful is a formal word, so it is used mostly in law and news.
exercise: «The judge said the arrest was wrongful, because the police had no proof.» What does wrongful mean here? | Kind and helpful | *Unfair and against the law | Brand new | Very loud
exercise: «Ava had been at school all day, so the accusation was wrongful.» Why was the accusation wrongful? | Ava was angry about it | The accusation was very long | Ava was at school, so she is clever | *Ava did not do it, so blaming her was unfair
exercise: Which phrase means being sacked from a job unfairly? | Happy holiday | Long walk | *Wrongful dismissal | Fresh bread
test: Which word means unfair or against the law? | Helpful | Colourful | *Wrongful | Careful
test: «The court said the sacking was wrongful, so the firm had to pay Jo.» What does wrongful tell us? | *The sacking was unfair | The sacking was fun | The sacking was early | The sacking was on a Monday
exam: «Ben was wrongfully arrested for a crime he did not commit.» What does wrongful arrest mean? | Arrested after a long chase | Arrested at a party | Arrested for a good reason | *Arrested unfairly, for something he did not do
